     tional login banner (e.g., _/_e_t_c_/_i_s_s_u_e).

     The classify entry is only valid for the default class as it is used
     prior to knowing who the user is.  The classify script may pass environ‐
     ment variables or other commands back to login(1) on file descriptor 3,
     just as an authentication program does.  The two variables AAUUTTHH__TTYYPPEE and
     RREEMMOOTTEE__NNAAMMEE are used to specify a new authentication type (the type must
     have the form auth-_t_y_p_e) and override the --hh option to login, respec‐
     tively.

